            "274": "s",
            "275": ".",
            "text": "<h3>Guiding Beyond Roadmaps</h3><p>Our principles served as the scaffolding for roadmap planning. Unlike timelines or feature lists, they weren’t bound to a quarter or release cycle. Instead, they were evergreen beliefs that guided investment decisions and gave us a consistent lens for evaluating success.</p><h3>Anchored in Seller Needs</h3><p>Each principle was rooted in what mattered most to Etsy sellers — clarity, trust, and efficiency in how their orders were fulfilled. By grounding the work this way, we ensured that strategic discussions didn’t drift into abstract debates but stayed connected to the realities of our community.</p><h3>A Leadership Tool</h3><p>For me as a design leader, these principles became more than just a design artifact. They gave product, engineering, and business leaders a shared language to align around. In practice, they acted as decision-making guardrails, helping teams prioritize tradeoffs with confidence while keeping the seller experience at the center.</p>",
            "title": ""
          },
          "column": "left"
        },
